rationale": "A three-way Republican field facing one well-funded Democrat, prediction markets near 75-78 percent Democratic, and a rating consensus tilting Democratic outweigh the state's Republican lean; the lone recent poll (D+3) and the fundraising gap point modestly to Kreiss-Tomkins.", "watch": "If Wilson or Bronson drops out and Republicans consolidate behind Taylor, the structural advantage flips and the race moves back toward a toss-up.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike Dunleavy (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Alaska's governorship is open as Republican Mike Dunleavy terms out, leaving one Democrat, Jonathan Kreiss-Tomkins, against three Republicans led by Treg Taylor, with Bernadette Wilson and Dave Bronson also on the ballot. The state leans Republican, but the divided GOP field and ranked-choice voting give the Democrat a structural edge. Cook, Sabato, DDHQ and Fox call it a toss-up; Inside Elections leans Republican, while RealClearPolitics leans Democratic and the Silver Bulletin rates it Safe Democratic.\n\nKreiss-Tomkins has raised about $2.2 million to Taylor's $880,000, and a national group recently added $650,000 to his effort. A September poll showed him ahead 43-40, though large swaths of the electorate remain undecided after a post-primary ballot shuffle restored Taylor to the race. Prediction markets price his chances near 75-78 percent, well above the ratings consensus.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6825, "margin": 2.46}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7335, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7395, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7331, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7068, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7071, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7313, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7365, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7094, "margin": 3.0}]}